# Fill in the details a catalog shows

Reading apps and online catalogs show a book's title, author, language and description. You set them in one place.

1. Click the [Book]{.ui} tab, then [Details]{.ui}.
2. Check the *Title*.
3. Under *Creators*, check each name and its role, such as [Author]{.ui} or [Illustrator]{.ui}. Click [Add Another Creator]{.ui} to add a name.
4. Check the language under *Languages*. It tells reading apps how to hyphenate the text and which voice to read it with.
5. Write a *Description* of a sentence or two.

Each change is saved when you leave the field. Package the book again to put the new details in the EPUB.

The publisher, rights and subjects are in Advanced Mode, under [Advanced details]{.ui}. To turn it on, click [Settings]{.ui}, then [General]{.ui}, and tick [Advanced mode]{.ui}.
